evidence was found for subscales of locus of control, the role of attribution of blame, spirituality, personality,      
appraisals, passive coping and emotion-focused coping. No evidence was found for an association between active          
problem-focused coping styles and QOL. CONCLUSION Many psychological factors were strongly and consistently related to  
